week pregnant, presents to the Emergency
Department with lower abdominal pain starting
few hours ago and increasing in intensity. Her
pregnancy so far has been uncomplicated, and
she is not on any medications apart from
supplements. Few days ago, she had an upper
respiratory infection associated with sneezing,
bouts of cough, runny nose, and mild fever from
which she is recovering. She denies vaginal
bleeding. On examination, her vitals are within
normal limits. Abdominal exam reveals
tenderness over the right lower part of her
uterus, but no abnormal uterine contractions are
note. A cardiotocograph (CTG) is normal with a
fetal heart rate of 155 bom. Which one of the
following could be the most likely explanation to
this presentation?','{"A":"Diastasis recti abdominis.","B":"Rectus sheath hematoma.","C":"Placental abruption.","D":"Placenta previa.","E":"Vasa previa. ©"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 OBS (2).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-087000803b2c","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"c32ab6ec25ab859b53b7","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 OBS (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 OBS (2).pdf","source_page":128,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"five_block_inferred","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"c32ab6ec25ab859b53b7","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 OBS (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 OBS (2).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":128,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Obstetrics","stem":"Janet, 32 years of age, who is 33-\nweek pregnant, presents to the Emergency\nDepartment with lower abdominal pain starting\nfew hours ago and increasing in intensity. Her\npregnancy so far has been uncomplicated, and\nshe is not on any medications apart from\nsupplements. Few days ago, she had an upper\nrespiratory infection associated with sneezing,\nbouts of cough, runny nose, and mild fever from\nwhich she is recovering. She denies vaginal\nbleeding. On examination, her vitals are within\nnormal limits. Abdominal exam reveals\ntenderness over the right lower part of her\nuterus, but no abnormal uterine contractions are\nnote. A cardiotocograph (CTG) is normal with a\nfetal heart rate of 155 bom. Which one of the\nfollowing could be the most likely explanation to\nthis presentation?","options":{"A":"Diastasis recti abdominis.","B":"Rectus sheath hematoma.","C":"Placental abruption.","D":"Placenta previa.","E":"Vasa previa. ©"},"source_answer":null,"sou